  {
    "episode_id": 70792,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70792.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 119,
    "turn_text": "Chad, my word is important. It's a rare attribute in politics we all know. And I use intention just because there could be a circumstance, I suppose, in which Democrats somehow nominate a leftist. If I don't think that person can win, I'll probably do what I did when I knew Joe Biden was not going to win and probably couldn't serve another four years, which is either work hard to recruit someone who can. And if all else fails, perhaps. I think it's a really unlikely scenario, and it is neither my interest. And I do think, like I said, Angie Craig, who is now the ranking member of the House Agriculture Committee, and most importantly, Chad, he's got private sector experience. And if I've learned a few things in Congress, it's that we, particularly Democrats, need people serving to understand how business operates how jobs are created and how policy affects our economy. And I'm just afraid too many Democrats right now don't have that experience. And she's one of the rare ones that does.",
