    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70792.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 121,
    "turn_text": "Well, to answer your first question, Chad, about the three aforementioned names, you know, they're all hypothetical right now. I do believe Angie Craig is not just qualified, but would be very able. And most importantly, in Minnesota, which is still a while we look blue to many, it's a state and the winds are blowing in the right direction. I think Angie Craig is the most likely Democrat to win that race. That is That's simply how I feel. As for running as Democrats, I made it very clear. I'm terribly disappointed in both parties. This is a duopoly that has a virtual monopoly on our electoral system. And if there's one attribute of the United States of America that I think should extend to politics, it's competition. And I think it's time for more. I'm spending time right now speaking with people all around the country about that shared interest. And this is Democrats and Republicans who recognize perhaps the greatest threat to our future is not a foreign threat but a domestic one. And it's the stranglehold of two parties on our politics.",
