    "turn_text": "No, I think it's time for somebody new. And I think eight years is plenty. I do believe in transitions. I believe in term limits. And it is my hope and expectation that others will step up and shed. I think We should start having a national conversation about attractive generation of potential leaders to public service, the erosion. of the public sector should be a concern to everybody, those on the right and those on the left. We see too many politicians demeaning government and those who work in it. We've seen an erosion of interest in becoming firefighters and police officers and certainly an erosion of those willing to step up and serve in government because of the attacks and of the difficult lifestyle. It even threats to one's life. And unless we start inspiring people to consider these paths and start attracting the best and brightest, rewarding them, and ensuring that those who do serve in these positions can manage, I think we're going to be in big trouble. So I believe Tim Walz to be a friend. I also believe that eight years should suffice and it's time for some change.",
