    "turn_idx": 143,
    "turn_text": "That's why I'm so chad. I'm incredulous because I'm watching my Republican colleagues just give him a hall pass and these are men and women who deeply value the rule of law as they should. I'm watching my Democratic colleagues, you know, do press conferences and put up their hands and object. without doing anything, without proposing an alternative, without joining the effort to reform government. By so doing, by the way, Chad, if Democrats would say that Donald Trump, you know what? We agree with a lot of what you're trying to do. Let's work together. But when it comes to USAID, which I believe to be the most important national defense mechanism that the United States has in its arsenal, when I think about the Department of Education, which needs to be reformed, but is integral to meaning some degree of standards and accountability and resource allocation to our schools. You can't just eliminate them at a wholesale level and expect our federal government to perform. But if Democrats are simply in front of microphones complaining, that is not a solution. And I'm really sick and tired of it. So I am disconcerted. And that's why I think I represent tens of millions of Americans who simply want some reason, common sense, and competency to solve problems. We haven't even talked about health care. Two thirds of Americans who declare bankruptcy because of medical. We haven't talked about our education system, which is so behind the rest of the developed world. And if we don't address these issues as Democrats and Republicans and Americans, we're going to need to do so with a new way forward. And that's why I'm hoping that those who are like minded share their ideas and we find a path forward. Simple as that.",
